| project _time, debug_event, reason, errorType, operationHash, eventType
| sort by _time desc | take 50
```

Follow one send/regenerate end to end by client span:

```apl
['chathub'] | where ['debug_namespace'] == 'chathub-generation-debug'
| extend payload=parse_json(extract("(\\{.*\\})$", 1, ['message']))
| extend spanId=tostring(payload.spanId), side=tostring(payload.side),
  outcome=tostring(payload.outcome), jobAdded=tobool(payload.jobAdded)
| where spanId == '<gd_span_id>'
| project _time, side, debug_event, outcome, reason=tostring(payload.reason),
  trpcCode=tostring(payload.trpcCode), jobAdded
| sort by _time asc
```

Generation-debug semantics:

- Client events (`side=client`) only appear when the server switch is on: the
  client gates on `GlobalServerConfig.generationDebug` (or the
  `localStorage['chathub.generationDebug']` override) and flushes through
  `conversationGeneration.reportClientDebug`, which re-sanitizes and re-emits.
- A healthy durable send is: `send_started` → `send_rpc_settled(outcome=ok,
  hasOperationId=true)` → `durable_attach` (client) → `enqueue_received` →
  `enqueue_persisted(jobAdded=true)` → `job_received` → `execute_started` →
  `execute_settled(outcome=succeeded)` → `event_applied_terminal` (client),
  all sharing one `spanId` where present.
- `send_rpc_settled(hasOperationId=false)` on a send that requested durable
  work must pair with server `enqueue_rejected` on the same `spanId`.
  `reason=unsupported_tool` includes `toolName`; `reason=fetch_on_client` is a
  missing server-reachable credential. Absence of that pair means the
  send-path drop was silent. `stillCurrent=false` / `topicChangedDuringRpc=true`
  means the user left during the send RPC (the known marker-not-created-yet
  race when `deferred_lane_marked` is also missing).
- A browser-fallback send that durable enqueue rejected must show
  `send_rpc_settled(hasOperationId=false, deferReason=…)` plus client
  `deferred_lane_marked` with the same `spanId`. `deferReason` and `reason`
  are readable labels (`unsupported_tool` is 16 characters and must not be
  hashed). After the user leaves that topic, `deferred_lane_left(producerAlive=true)` should appear. The healthy
  off-screen path is then `tool_loop_continue` (`visible=false` is OK) on the
  same `spanId` **before** they return. After they return,
  `deferred_lane_resumed` is `still_producing` if that continue already
  started, or `resume_model` / `resume_tools` /
  `deferred_placeholder_finalized` only as a backup. `sync_summary.reason`
  names why sync ran (`topic_change` / `visibility` / …).
  `topic_busy_changed(outcome=busy)` should bracket the topic-list spinner
  for that hashed topic.
- After a successful MCP/tool batch, look for `tool_loop_continue` on the same
  `spanId` even while the user is on another topic. Absence plus
  `tool_loop_continue_skipped` is the stall:
  `reason=no_resumable_tool` (results cancelled/empty), `batch_gated` (left
  before the batch started and there was no deferred lane),
  `session_changed` / `not_visible` (continue gated after tools finished).
  `no_resumable_tool` with `cancelledCount>=1` and `completedCount=0` right
  after a persisted MCP **or builtin** result on leave is the abort-on-switch
  regression (topic switch must not abort deferred-conversation tool
  controllers, RAG loading, or rewrite a persist as cancelled). Outcome counts
  (`completedCount`, `cancelledCount`) are hashes-free.
  `invalidate_preserved` on leave should keep plugin/RAG/search/chat-loading
  counts for the deferred conversation (`preserved*Count>=1` with matching
  `aborted*Count` only for other topics). `rag_retrieve_settled` on the same
  `spanId` is `ok`/`empty` after leave; `hard_cancelled` is Stop. Leave during
  retrieve must log `deferred_lane_left(producerAlive=true)` because the
  assistant stays on `chatLoadingIds` (or the user RAG row stays in
  `messageRAGLoadingIds`). `producerAlive=false` plus `rag_retrieve_settled(ok)`
  is the empty-Reference-Source hang. Join builtin
  search with `builtin_tool_settled` (`toolName=lobe-web-browsing`,
  `visible=false`, hashed session/topic of the **left** conversation — not
  the topic you clicked). `message_persist_skipped(reason=not_visible)` after
  leave is the persist-context regression; `hard_cancelled` is Stop / account
  switch.
  `deferred_lane_resumed(outcome=still_producing)` now includes
  `chatLoading` / `toolsCalling` / `streamActive` / `pendingModelContinue` /
  `pendingTools` so a leaked tools-calling flag is visible without dumping
  message ids. `sync_summary.resumedModel` is true when return sync itself
  called `triggerAIMessage`.
- A search-only send with Code Interpreter enabled must `enqueue_persisted`,
  not `enqueue_rejected` / `toolName=lobe-code-interpreter`. If the worker
  actually invokes CI, look for `sandbox_run_settled(outcome=ok|error|…)`
  then the model continue. DALL·E stubs still emit
  `browser_tool_stubbed(toolName=…, shouldContinue=false)`. Continue /
  tool-loop fetches emit `exec_runtime_settled(kind=continue)` on the same
  `spanId`.
- A leftover iOS/Safari chat-stream death is
  `fetch_stream_interrupted(errorKind=webkit_load_failed, classifiedAs=abort,
  hasOutput=true|false)` — not `fetch_stream_error` and not
  `UnknownChatFetchError`. Chromium's equivalent is
  `errorKind=failed_to_fetch`. Do not treat `sse_client_stream_failed`
  (`errorType=TypeError`) as the chat-summary fetch; that event is the SSE
  reconnect.
- `enqueue_persisted(jobAdded=false)` does not occur on the transactional send
  path (a failed SQL add rolls the enqueue back); the false path lives in
  `sweep_reenqueued`, where it means an operation row exists but no Graphile
  job could be added — the sweeper will retry on its next pass.
- Worker health: `worker_started` appears once per container boot; its absence
  with `worker_start_failed` means the Graphile runner never came up and no
  job will run until restart. `job_malformed` means a queued payload lacked
  `operationId`/`userId` and was dropped. `sweep_failed` names the failing
  sweep phase (`initial`/`periodic`).
- Queue latency: `job_received.queueAgeMs` measures Graphile claim delay;
  `execute_started.queueAgeMs` measures operation-row age at claim. Large
  values with a healthy worker mean queue backlog, not a stuck job.
- Delivery: `sse_opened`/`sse_closed` bracket each server SSE connection
  (`deliveredCount` counts events written, `reason=abort|error`); `sse_reset`
  marks a cursor reset + replay. Client-side `sse_client_stream_ended` /
  `sse_client_stream_failed` mark reconnect episodes, `sse_client_poll_failed`
  is throttled to the first failure per episode, and
  `sse_client_reset_replay` reports replayed event counts.
- Client drops: `event_dropped(reason=not_attached|stale_revision)` means the
  browser received an event it could not apply. Snapshot drops are throttled
  to one per operation+reason; `done`/`error` drops are always logged and are
  the smoking gun for "server finished but the reply never appeared".
  `event_applied_terminal` is the positive counterpart proving end-to-end
  delivery of a terminal event.
- `execute_transcript_loaded` is emitted from `loadScopedMessages` for chat,
  title, compaction, and supervisor loads. It carries `transcriptCount`,
  `omitSessionFilter`, `persistedSessionNull`, `hasTopicId`, plus
  `parentUserHash` (content hash of the triggering user message) and
  `lastTranscriptUserHash` (last user message in the loaded transcript). A
  hash mismatch proves a transcript/binding race. `transcriptCount=0` on a
  title job is an empty load, not a missing worker.
- `execute_retrying` fires when `markForRetry` succeeds. For empty title
  transcripts ChatHub then schedules a delayed Graphile job (seconds, not
  20–50ms) and does **not** rethrow, so Graphile's default retry is not the
  backoff. Other retryable errors still rethrow so Graphile owns the job.
  `errorClass` names the throw (for example `TitleTranscriptEmptyError`). Do
  not treat it as `sweep_reenqueued`. Empty compaction summaries are **not**
  this path: they skip `markForRetry`, finalize `failed` with
  `EmptyCompactionSummaryError`, and log `provider` plus numeric
  `contentChars` / `reasoningChars` on `execute_settled`. Built-in model-bank
  IDs stay readable under `model`; custom/unlisted model IDs are fingerprinted.
- `execute_settled` is terminal only; retries do not emit it.
  `execute_started` / `execute_retrying` / `execute_settled` keep `provider`
  readable. `model` is readable only when it matches a built-in model-bank id.
  Session/topic ids stay hashed.
- `regenerate_early_return` names the guard that made Regenerate a no-op
  (`reason=noAnchor|retrying|notCurrent`).
- `sync_summary` reports per-sync counts plus `reason` (`topic_change` /
  `visibility` / …), `deferredLaneCount`, `resumedTools`, and `resumedModel`.
  `orphan_deleted`
  records the cleanup of stale `...` placeholder rows. Join leave/return with
  `deferred_lane_*` on the same `spanId` as `send_rpc_settled`.
  `deferred_placeholder_finalized` means persist already wrote content and
  sync cleared the deferred marker. It must not fire for leftover
  `LOADING_FLAT` rows.
- Chat Image tool tiles (`lobe-image-designer`) share this
  `chathub-generation-debug` stream, not `CHATHUB_IMAGE_DEBUG`. Join
  `chat_image_run_started` / `chat_image_item_settled` /
  `chat_image_run_settled` to the send `spanId`. Readable `outcome` values:
  run `ok` / `partial` / `failed` / `no_origin` / `already_done` /
  `no_model` / `persist_unproven` / `not_current`; item `attached` /
  `failed` / `not_current` / `persist_unproven` / `skipped`. `visible=false`
  after leave is expected. Server `chat_image_task_created(outcome=inserted)`
  is the billable insert; `idempotent` is a same-id retry; `chat_image_task_rejected(outcome=uncorrelated)`
  means the message no longer carried that unresolved task. Diagnose:
  `fetch_stream_interrupted(errorKind=webkit_load_failed)` with **no**
  `chat_image_run_started` on that `spanId` is Safari abort during think
  (tools never started — [iOS fetch "Load failed"](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/71280168));
  `persist_unproven` or missing `attached` after `visible=false` is the
  origin-map persist bug; `created=true` plus `task_created` then no
  `attached` is poll/attach, not persist.

Tool-call failures:

```apl
['chathub'] | where ['debug_namespace'] == 'chathub-tools-debug'
  and ['debug_event'] endswith '_failed'
| extend payload=parse_json(extract("(\\{.*\\})$", 1, ['message']))
| extend diagnosticId=tostring(payload.diagnosticId), spanId=tostring(payload.spanId),
