| sort by spanId asc, eventSequence asc
```

`eventSequence` is monotonic inside one `spanId`; the browser failure report is a second span carrying the same `diagnosticId`.

`transport_request_retry` is recovery telemetry, not a terminal failure. For example, `reason=oauth_unauthorized` with HTTP 401 is healthy when the same `diagnosticId` later has `oauth_operation_complete` with `outcome=refreshed`, then `transport_request_complete` HTTP 200 and `tools_rpc_complete` HTTP 200.

Detect a downstream proxy replacement: compare `tools_rpc_complete.response.responseFingerprint` with `client_rpc_response_failed.responseFingerprint` for the same `diagnosticId`. Different fingerprints or server-side `bodyKind=json` followed by client-side `bodyKind=html` indicate that something after ChatHub replaced the response.

## Verify the env var is actually live

Absence of `debug_namespace=chathub-tools-debug` or `debug_namespace=chathub-image-debug` records almost always means the var is not in the running container or the image predates structured diagnostics — not an app bug.

```bash
docker inspect lobe-chat --format '{{.Config.Image}}'
docker exec lobe-chat env | grep CHATHUB_TOOLS_DEBUG # must print the value
docker exec lobe-chat env | grep CHATHUB_IMAGE_DEBUG # must print the value
docker exec lobe-chat env | grep CHATHUB_GENERATION_DEBUG # must print the value
docker exec lobe-chat sh -c 'cat /proc/1/environ | tr "\0" "\n" | grep CHATHUB_TOOLS_DEBUG'
docker exec lobe-chat sh -c 'cat /proc/1/environ | tr "\0" "\n" | grep CHATHUB_IMAGE_DEBUG'
docker exec lobe-chat sh -c 'cat /proc/1/environ | tr "\0" "\n" | grep CHATHUB_GENERATION_DEBUG'
docker exec lobe-chat sh -c 'cat /proc/1/environ | tr "\0" "\n" | grep -E "DEBUG_.*_CACHE|KEY_VAULTS_SECRET|NEXT_AUTH_SECRET"'
```

`/proc/1/environ` reads the live server process env — most authoritative. After changing the var, recreate: `docker compose up -d --force-recreate chathub`.

## Healthy signals

- Tools: an MCP call should end with `call_tool_complete` and `tools_rpc_complete` HTTP 200 for the same `diagnosticId`, ordered by per-span `eventSequence`. Cold connections may also show `client_initialized`; warm calls commonly show `client_cache_lookup` with `outcome=hit` and no initialization event. Safe technical tool/procedure labels may be readable, but arguments, results, bodies, arbitrary errors, credentials, query strings, environment values, and user/connection identifiers must never be raw.
- Image workspace (`CHATHUB_IMAGE_DEBUG`): one `/image` submission should show `submission_accepted`, `batch_persisted`, `dispatch_started`, paired `async_route_started`/`async_route_settled`, provider events, transform/upload events, and terminal `task_status_settled`. Safe records may show provider hashes, dimensions, status/media metadata, counts, and keyed hashes, but provider labels, prompts, image URLs/data, response bodies, user/database IDs, credentials, headers/cookies, arbitrary error messages, stacks, and environment values must never be raw. Chat Image tool tiles are generation-debug (`chat_image_*`), not this stream.
- Tool lifecycle: every local batch should have `tool_batch_started`, one `tool_completion_reported` per expected call, and `tool_batch_settled`. `resultCount + failureCount` should equal `toolCallCount`. Provider-native tools are `delegated`/`handed_off`; ChatHub built-ins are `builtin`.
- Cache: every enabled request should have one `request` followed by one `usage`, `usage_missing`, or `terminal_error` for the same `requestHash`. `cachedTokens=0` is an explicit zero only when the provider reported it. Missing cache counters or `cacheStatus=not_reported` are unavailable telemetry, not misses.
- Generation: every durable send/regenerate should show one `enqueue_persisted` with `jobAdded=true`, then `job_received`, one `execute_started` and one `execute_settled` for the same `operationHash`, and a client `event_applied_terminal` for the same `operationHash` when the browser was open. Client `send_*`/`regenerate_*`/`sync_summary` events with the same `spanId` bracket the server events. A search-only send with Code Interpreter enabled must not show `enqueue_rejected` / `lobe-code-interpreter`. A CI invoke must show `sandbox_run_settled` (not `browser_tool_stubbed`). A leftover Safari chat stream that dies must show `fetch_stream_interrupted(errorKind=webkit_load_failed)` and must not persist `UnknownChatFetchError`. Continue fetches emit `exec_runtime_settled(kind=continue)`. Worker DALL·E stubs emit `browser_tool_stubbed`. A browser-fallback chat Image turn that actually starts tiles must show `chat_image_run_started` then per-index `chat_image_item_settled(outcome=attached)` and `chat_image_run_settled(outcome=ok)` on that `spanId` (`visible=false` after leave is OK), plus server `chat_image_task_created` when a billable insert happens. Absence of `chat_image_run_started` after `webkit_load_failed` means tools never started. A send that requested durable work but stayed in the browser must show `send_rpc_settled(hasOperationId=false)` paired with server `enqueue_rejected` on that `spanId`, with a readable `deferReason`. Title empty-transcript retries emit `execute_retrying` rather than `execute_settled`. One `worker_started` should appear per container boot. Identifiers appear only as sha256-16 hashes; message content, session/topic ids, and error messages must never be raw.
